; An embedder seed written before the run must survive the start-audio
; bootstrap. `gain` is read only by the audio thread (audience
; audio+external, no main bit), so the main thread's replica of it is
; never authoritative — the bootstrap's force-publish must not clobber the
; embedder's pre-run seed with main's stale zeros. The audio replica's
; first adopt must see the seeded value, and no main-publish of `gain`
; may appear anywhere. (This is exactly easl-studio's startup sequence:
; seed the sliders, run, start-audio — regression-pinned after it shipped
; silent-until-slider-drag.)
@external @local
(var gain: f32
     0.)

@audio
(defn f [t: f32
         rate: f32]: f32
  gain)

@cpu
(defn main []
  (spawn-window (fn []
                    (start-audio f))))
